templates.body:
Format these encounter notes as a SOAP note. Do not add findings, diagnoses, medications or doses I did not write; where something is missing, write [not documented]. Keep units exactly as given.

Patient reference: {{patient_ref}}
Encounter date: {{encounter_date}}
Setting: {{setting}}

Notes:
{{notes}}

Draft a discharge summary from the notes: reason for admission, hospital course, procedures, condition at discharge, discharge medications (only those listed, with the doses I gave), follow-up appointments, and instructions for the patient in plain language. Flag every item you could not find as [confirm].

Patient reference: {{patient_ref}}
Admission: {{admission_date}} · Discharge: {{discharge_date}}

Notes:
{{notes}}

Write a referral letter to {{specialist}} about {{patient_ref}}: reason for referral, relevant history and current medications as I list them, investigations to date, and the specific question I want answered ({{question}}). Formal, concise, one page.

Clinical details:
{{details}}

Turn these clinical instructions into after-visit instructions for the patient at about a {{reading_level}} reading level in {{language}}. Short sentences, headings for What to do, What to watch for, When to seek help. Do not add advice beyond what I wrote.

Instructions:
{{instructions}}
